{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":214718,"duration_api_ms":359388,"ttft_ms":14932,"ttft_stream_ms":8838,"time_to_request_ms":30,"num_turns":28,"result":"## Summary\n\nCustom extension repository URLs are now validated before any network call:\n\n- **`domain/.../model/InvalidExtensionStoreUrlException.kt`** (new) — marker exception, following the same pattern as `NoChaptersException`.\n- **`domain/.../interactor/AddExtensionStore.kt`** — before delegating to `repository.insert()` (which triggers the network fetch), parses the URL with `java.net.URI` and rejects it unless the scheme is `http`/`https` and a host is present. Covers empty input, missing scheme, wrong scheme, and malformed text.\n- **`ExtensionStoresViewModel.kt`** — catches `InvalidExtensionStoreUrlException` specifically and shows a friendly, localized message instead of the raw exception text; all other failure paths (network errors, parse errors) are unchanged.\n- **`strings.xml`** — added `extensionStoresScreen.addStore.invalidUrl`: \"This isn't a valid repository URL. Enter a link that starts with http:// or https://\".\n\nThis applies to both the manual \"add repo\" dialog and the deep-link add flow, since both go through `AddExtensionStore`. Adding, refreshing, and removing valid repos is untouched. Verified `:domain:compileDebugKotlin` and `:app:compileDebugKotlin` both build cleanly with these changes.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3b2f4014-f1ee-4d31-bd59-570cfb2c68c6","total_cost_usd":1.7989729499999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38985,"cache_read_input_tokens":1668741,"output_tokens":15315,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38985,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":107,"outputTokens":290